---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Projects & Contributions — Rithika Silva" description="A non-exhaustive list of public projects and contributions by Rithika Silva from outside his day-to-day work.">
  <main>
    <a href="/">&larr; Home</a>

    <header>
      <h1>Projects &amp; Contributions</h1>
      <p>A non-exhaustive sample of public projects and contributions from outside my day-to-day work.</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="open-source">
      <h2 id="open-source">Open Source</h2>
      <div>
        <article>
          <h3>
            <a href="https://github.com/catppuccin/blink" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Catppuccin for Blink Shell</a>
          </h3>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>U SPORTS Data Packages</h3>
          <p>
            Primarily developed
            <a href="https://github.com/uwaggs/usportspy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">usportspy</a>
            (Python) and contributed to
            <a href="https://uwaggs.github.io/usportsR/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">usportsR</a>
            (R). Led data acquisition.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="earlier-work">
      <h2 id="earlier-work">Earlier Work</h2>
      <article>
        <h3>Sports Data at Waterloo</h3>
        <p>
          Built sports-data infrastructure and analysis tools. Co-authored
          <a href="https://ww2.amstat.org/meetings/jsm/2026/onlineprogram/abstract.cfm?sid=7077&amp;tid=7172" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Accessible and Cost-Effective Data Science Infrastructure for Collegiate Sports Analytics</a>,
          a paper presented at JSM 2026.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>
          <a href="https://academic.oup.com/jrssig/article/21/3/6/7686552" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Peaks and Primes: Do Athletes Get One Shot at Glory?</a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Provided data-acquisition support for this
          <a href="https://academic.oup.com/jrssig" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><em>Significance</em></a> study of Olympic track-and-field athletes’
          peak-performance windows.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>


  </main>
</Layout>
